{"h":3106,"w":2400,"lines":[{"h":0.018528202005301697,"c":1,"x":0.13332195848975051,"t":"Introduction","y":0.064863805951719034,"w":0.11305533091227216},{"t":"MARKING THE PRACTICE TESTS","y":0.11317849656239776,"w":0.41189631144205735,"c":1,"h":0.020648826112765639,"x":0.13521765383718426},{"c":1,"t":"Listening and Reading","w":0.23931068420410156,"x":0.13319119432593235,"y":0.1494115165833152,"h":0.022259095063611789},{"w":0.35388559977213541,"y":0.17684752781538615,"t":"The Answer Keys are on pages 118-125.","h":0.020109225762558247,"c":1,"x":0.13321735800887771},{"h":0.017707662588538287,"t":"Each question in the Listening and Reading tests is worth one mark.","y":0.19607211821101866,"c":1,"x":0.13345864142983335,"w":0.58082707722981775},{"w":0.50776423136393234,"t":"Questions which require letter \/ Roman numeral answers","h":0.020798758698983622,"c":1,"x":0.13334784982632319,"y":0.23247654514315597},{"h":0.022124905165594289,"c":1,"w":0.76718475341796877,"x":0.1314430139165097,"t":"• For questions where the answers are letters or Roman numerals, you should write only","y":0.25515738882631434},{"c":1,"t":"the number of answers required. For example, if the answer is a single letter or numeral","x":0.15771068982129074,"h":0.024609862338015098,"y":0.27214597330369839,"w":0.7484798685709636},{"w":0.74078913370768218,"h":0.020276383438650791,"c":1,"y":0.29243328315210415,"x":0.15780869698498626,"t":"you should write only one answer. If you have written more letters or numerals than are"},{"w":0.38557619730631509,"t":"required, the answer must be marked wrong.","x":0.15591116142068187,"h":0.019854931852852808,"y":0.31016914054725764,"c":1},{"w":0.58668909708658845,"t":"Questions which require answers in the form of words or numbers","c":1,"y":0.34876279389253084,"h":0.019575240607424438,"x":0.13334498492176125},{"t":"• Answers may be written in upper or lower case.","c":1,"x":0.12946356511774681,"y":0.37092266278932162,"w":0.43469711303710934,"h":0.020388364331306197},{"t":"• Words in brackets are optional - they are correct, but not necessary.","c":1,"h":0.022780878345811328,"y":0.38855598929474011,"w":0.61128316243489578,"x":0.12952588663808248},{"y":0.40813982449459874,"c":1,"w":0.44205688476562499,"x":0.12955030758712013,"h":0.01852123459461652,"t":"• Alternative answers are separated by a slash (\/)."},{"w":0.69375539143880216,"h":0.018502333052144548,"x":0.1296275508069569,"c":1,"t":"• If you are asked to write an answer using a certain number of words and\/or (a)","y":0.42720717039724554},{"w":0.74270416259765626,"h":0.021475576387246953,"t":"number(s), you will be penalised if you exceed this. For example, if a question specifies","y":0.44467865872331958,"c":1,"x":0.15589938331620468},{"h":0.018433840445219341,"t":"an answer using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS and the correct answer is 'black","x":0.15594980038640452,"w":0.72006413777669276,"y":0.46302838646002242,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"leather coat, the answer 'coat of black leather' is incorrect.","x":0.15399035550241597,"w":0.50029200236002591,"h":0.021914514663214812,"y":0.47894985301669157},{"x":0.12774664974668126,"y":0.5010164312947909,"t":"• In questions where you are expected to complete a gap, you should only transfer the","w":0.74637878417968762,"h":0.018549733060602147,"c":1},{"w":0.74274709065755218,"h":0.021251376336878236,"t":"necessary missing word(s) onto the answer sheet. For example, to complete 'in the ...,","x":0.1540092934302148,"y":0.51773939829048876,"c":1},{"x":0.15413532617986447,"w":0.72368423461914066,"h":0.017707662588538287,"c":1,"y":0.53766902761393265,"t":"where the correct answer is 'morning', the answer 'in the morning' would be incorrect"},{"t":"• All answers require correct spelling (including words in brackets)","w":0.57733469645182289,"x":0.12768736194200045,"y":0.55495132658332313,"h":0.019171296590693276,"c":1},{"w":0.68074727376302091,"c":1,"h":0.021495394144838142,"t":"• Both US and UK spelling are acceptable and are included in the Answer Key.","y":0.57161861056644703,"x":0.12768369192491283},{"h":0.022551274345677941,"t":"• All standard alternatives for numbers, dates and currencies are acceptable.","c":1,"x":0.12764535731533053,"w":0.66764806111653641,"y":0.59018756272147832},{"h":0.01859341294091521,"t":"• All standard abbreviations are acceptable.","y":0.60842720633308456,"x":0.12763863910876619,"c":1,"w":0.38762598673502602},{"x":0.12573129242663109,"w":0.64893961588541671,"h":0.02369754051901185,"t":"• You will find additional notes about individual answers in the Answer Key.","y":0.6247054372233688,"c":1},{"t":"Writing","h":0.023597732023201146,"x":0.12814032627036756,"c":1,"y":0.65479580508067337,"w":0.080496667226155616},{"w":0.78784434000651038,"h":0.022157928211337441,"t":"The sample answers are on pages 126-135. It is not possible for you to give yourself a mark","y":0.68369342115654008,"c":1,"x":0.12769432573676795},{"c":1,"t":"for the Writing tasks. We have provided sample answers (written by candidates), showing","w":0.75962015787760406,"x":0.12582955880756355,"h":0.020524110935306927,"y":0.70260299016731353},{"y":0.71932089323563708,"w":0.7596936543782552,"h":0.022738722624966123,"c":1,"t":"their score and the examiner's comments. These sample answers will give you an insight","x":0.12579668128058},{"t":"into what is required for the Writing test.","y":0.73883488271098674,"w":0.3443882751464844,"h":0.018911300285815891,"x":0.12386225756479709,"c":1}]}